.2,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0040517417021527224,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":55.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.07668838234670661,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00777,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Rambus Inc. manufactures and sells semiconductor products in the United States, South Korea, Singapore, and internationally. It offers memory interface chips comprising DDR5 memory interface chips which include registering clock driver, multiplexed registering clock driver, multiplexed data buffer, power management integrated circuits, serial presence detect hubs, temperature sensors, and client clock driver products; and DDR4 memory interface chips. The company also provides silicon IP, such as interface and security IP solutions that move and protect data in advanced artificial intelligence, data center, government, and automotive applications; interface IP solutions for high-speed memory and chip-to-chip digital controller IP; security IP solutions, including crypto cores, hardware roots of trust, high-speed protocol engines, and chip provisioning technologies. In addition, it offers portfolio of patents that covers memory architecture, high-speed serial links, and security products. The company sells its products to memory module manufacturers, OEMs and hyperscalers, as well as to chip makers. It markets its products and services through its direct sales force and distributors. Rambus Inc. was incorporated in 1990 and is headquartered in San Jose, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Luc  Seraphin | CEO, President & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 791 people. Revenue per employee of $895K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 5%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $421K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $69K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Rambus, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $7.1B market cap on $708M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +16% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are contracting by -2.2pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 26% against a 12% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 78% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $333M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 47 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.56\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins softening -2.2pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Carries a 42% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.41730197699961247},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $14.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (43% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 19.3% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 26% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 30% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Rambus, Inc. (NASDAQ:RMBS) Stock Now Rated \u201cModerate Buy\u201d by Sell-Side Brokerages","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/rambus-inc-nasdaqrmbs-stock-now-rated-moderate-buy-by-sell-side-brokerages.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795167049.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.765,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"29,472 Rambus, Inc. $RMBS Shares Sold by Retirement Systems of Alabama","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/29472-rambus-inc-rmbs-shares-sold-by-retirement-systems-of-alabama